LiquidLaneRedeemCapability
├── factory initialization and migration
│   ├── rejects zero adapter, protocol, and Reactor without code
│   ├── preserves request funding and signatures across state-preserving migrations
│   └── rejects migration data and a different immutable Reactor
├── signRequest
│   ├── requires the bound adapter through a Merkle leaf role
│   ├── rejects zero or unlimited input, expiry, and empty signatures
│   ├── binds the configured protocol and positive outputs to the adapter
│   ├── allows one outstanding request per input token and per consumer nonce
│   ├── rejects consumed Reactor nonces and inexact transfer funding
│   └── pulls and approves exactly the signed input amount
├── isValidSignature
│   ├── rejects absent, empty, mismatched, expired, revoked, and consumed signatures
│   ├── binds every field and output-array hash to the upstream Reactor request
│   └── rejects another chain, Reactor, or capability
├── Reactor fill through LiquidLaneAdapter
│   ├── transfers the capability's input and delivers each output directly to the Merkle adapter
│   ├── consumes the capability-owned nonce and exact allowance
│   └── atomically rolls back a fill that cannot deliver its signed output
├── revokeRequest
│   ├── requires the adapter and a known request
│   ├── invalidates both the signature and Reactor nonce
│   └── succeeds even when token transfers and approvals are paused
└── finalizeRequest
    ├── requires the adapter and a known finished request
    ├── refuses to release funding at the inclusive expiry boundary
    ├── clears allowance before returning remaining input and unsolicited transfers
    └── clears only the finalized token and nonce so unrelated requests remain valid
